  "_note": [
    "Board 149:50, reached from the root by the panel's own row click — see the",
    "content-root recipe for why the manager is stubbed and everything above it is",
    "the shipped code.",
    "",
    "BOARD won once: 149:57 states 12/18 on the meta STRIP, not only on the two",
    "words inside it. The strip was inheriting the document's 16 — invisible while",
    "both children override it, and wrong the moment anything else lands in the row.",
    "The record rows and the two footer List rows needed nothing beyond the",
    "232:6 / 240:14 line-heights already landed for content-root.",
    "",
    "ONE UNKNOWN, deliberately left: 233:1309 (the Dynamic pages row) states",
    "line-height 20 on the ROW, and its twin 233:1304 on the same board does not.",
    "That is Figma hoisting a text style to the parent when an instance's children",
    "all share it — the Dynamic pages instance has no count, the Fields one does.",
    "The DOM row paints no text of its own, so there is nothing to compare; making",
    "it pass would mean putting a line-height on chrome-ui Row's `default` size,",
    "which every family's rows share and no other board asks for.",
    "",
    "NOT anchored: 149:50 the board frame (drawer chrome), 149:55 / the Back row",
    "frame at 36 — Crumb is an h-8 Button inside a my-0.5 margin, which is the same",
    "36 the board draws, but as margin+control rather than one 36 box, and the",
    "control is anchored on its own at 149:56. Three hotspot/* nodes.",
    "",
    "BOARD-COPY: 4 leads, none drift. \"‹ Menu items\" and \"4 records\" render",
    "exactly (read back from the DOM); the checker splits them because JSX emits",
    "`‹ {label}` and `{n} record{s}` as separate text nodes. The board's own \"24\"",
    "is sample data against a 4-record fixture."
